{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"566","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"F. Clique in the Divisibility Graph"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"As you must know, the maximum clique problem in an arbitrary graph is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"NP"},{"kind":"text","text":"-hard. Nevertheless, for some graphs of specific kinds it can be solved effectively."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Just in case, let us remind you that a clique in a non-directed graph is a subset of the vertices of a graph, such that any two vertices of this subset are connected by an edge. In particular, an empty set of vertexes and a set consisting of a single vertex, are cliques."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's define a divisibility graph for a set of positive integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"A = {a1, a2, ..., an}"},{"kind":"text","text":" as follows. The vertices of the given graph are numbers from set "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"A"},{"kind":"text","text":", and two numbers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"aj"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i ≠ j"},{"kind":"text","text":") are connected by an edge if and only if either "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai"},{"kind":"text","text":" is divisible by "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"aj"},{"kind":"text","text":", or "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"aj"},{"kind":"text","text":" is divisible by "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given a set of non-negative integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"A"},{"kind":"text","text":". Determine the size of a maximum clique in a divisibility graph for set "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"A"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ n ≤ 106"},{"kind":"text","text":"), that sets the size of set "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"A"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" distinct positive integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a1, a2, ..., an"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ ai ≤ 106"},{"kind":"text","text":") — elements of subset "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"A"},{"kind":"text","text":". The numbers in the line follow in the ascending order."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print a single number — the maximum size of a clique in a divisibility graph for set "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"A"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"8\n3 4 6 8 10 18 21 24\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first sample test a clique of size 3 is, for example, a subset of vertexes "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"{3, 6, 18}"},{"kind":"text","text":". A clique of a larger size doesn't exist in this graph."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"F","problemCode":"566F","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/566/problem/F"}